        <qualifiedname>QAccelPlot::LineStroke::verticesPerPathPoint</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>splitJoins</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns the ribbon vertices of a path point: four with <emphasis>splitJoins</emphasis>, or two otherwise. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Split joins give a path point one vertex pair that ends the segment before it and one that starts the segment after it, so a join too sharp for a miter draws as a bevel. Without them, both segments share a mitered pair, which suits paths that only turn by right angles. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
